---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT, LEGAL } from '../consts';

const addr = CONTACT.address;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Diamond Recruiters collects, uses, shares and retains personal information, and the rights you have over it."
>
  <section class="border-b border-ink-100 bg-ink-950">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-14 pt-16 lg:px-8 lg:pb-16 lg:pt-24">
      <p class="eyebrow text-ice-400">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl leading-tight text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-ink-300">Last updated: {LEGAL.policyLastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14 lg:px-8 lg:py-20">
    <div
      class="mb-12 rounded-2xl border border-copper-500/30 bg-copper-500/8 px-6 py-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-800"
    >
      <p class="font-medium text-copper-500">Before this page goes live</p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        This policy is a complete, working draft written for a US-incorporated recruitment
        business. The company identifiers below are still placeholders, and the text has not
        been reviewed by an attorney. Fill in the real entity details in
        <code class="rounded bg-ink-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">src/consts.ts</code>
        and have counsel review it before you publish.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-dr text-ink-700">
      <p>
        {LEGAL.entityName} (&ldquo;{SITE.name}&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) is a
        recruitment business operating at <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.domain}</a>. This policy
        explains what personal information we collect, why we collect it, who we share it
        with, and what you can ask us to do with it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {LEGAL.entityName}, a {LEGAL.entityType} organized in {LEGAL.stateOfIncorporation}.
        Postal address: {addr.line1}, {addr.city}, {addr.region} {addr.postalCode},
        {' '}{addr.countryName}. You can reach us about anything on this page at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.general}`}>{CONTACT.general}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect only what we need to do recruitment work. In practice that means:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you give us directly</strong> — your name, email address,
          telephone number, base city, salary expectation, willingness to travel, LinkedIn
          profile, the contents of your resume, and anything else you choose to write in a
          message to us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Information about a hiring need</strong> — if you contact us as an
          employer, your name, work email, telephone number, company, and the details of
          the role you are hiring for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Information from public and professional sources</strong> — where we
          identify potential candidates through professional networking sites, company
          websites, industry directories and referrals. If we approach you this way we will
          tell you where we found you if you ask.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Basic technical information</strong> — when you submit a form we record
          the submission time and the IP address it came from, purely to prevent abuse of
          the form.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To assess whether you are a fit for a role and to discuss that with you</li>
        <li>
          To present you to a prospective employer — <strong
            >only after you have approved that specific employer by name</strong
          >
        </li>
        <li>To contact you about roles that may be relevant to you in future</li>
        <li>To respond to an enquiry you have sent us</li>
        <li>To keep records of the work we have done for a client</li>
        <li>To protect our forms from automated abuse</li>
        <li>To meet legal, tax and regulatory obligations</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it with advertisers or data
        brokers.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Prospective employers</strong>, and only with your prior approval for that
          named company. If you tell us there is an employer you do not want approached, we
          block it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Service providers</strong> who host our website and handle our email. They
          process information on our instructions only.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Authorities</strong>, where we are legally required to disclose something.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep candidate information for as long as it is useful for finding you a role,
        and review it periodically. If you ask us to delete your information we will do so,
        except where we are required to retain records — for example where a placement has
        been made and we need the record for tax or contractual purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Whoever and wherever you are, you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Tell you what information we hold about you</li>
        <li>Give you a copy of it</li>
        <li>Correct anything that is wrong</li>
        <li>Delete it</li>
        <li>Stop contacting you</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.general}`}>{CONTACT.general}</a> and we will action it.
        We will not treat you differently for exercising any of these rights.
      </p>

      <h3>If you are a California resident</h3>
      <p>
        Under the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended by the CPRA, you additionally
        have the right to know the categories of personal information we have collected, the
        purposes for collecting it, and the categories of third parties we disclose it to —
        all of which are set out above. You have the right to request deletion or
        correction, and the right to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information.
        <strong>We do not sell or share personal information as those terms are defined
        under the CCPA</strong>, so there is nothing to opt out of. You may use an
        authorized agent to make a request on your behalf.
      </p>

      <h3>If you are in the European Economic Area or the UK</h3>
      <p>
        Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies to our processing, our lawful bases are your
        consent (where you submitted a form) and our legitimate interest in carrying out
        recruitment activity. You may withdraw consent at any time, and you have the right
        to lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served over HTTPS and form submissions are transmitted encrypted.
        Resumes you upload are emailed directly to our recruitment inbox and are not stored
        on the web server. No system is perfectly secure, but we limit what we collect and
        who can reach it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website sets no advertising or tracking cookies and does not use third-party
        analytics. Fonts and images are served from our own domain, so browsing the site
        does not report your visit to anyone else.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is aimed at working professionals. We do not knowingly collect information
        from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has sent us information, contact us and
        we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy we will update the date at the top of this page. Material
        changes will be highlighted on the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy, or a request about your information:{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.general}`}>{CONTACT.general}</a>, or write to us at the
        postal address above.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
